{"id": "EUVD-2026-86697", "enisaUuid": "41dcd92b-1054-3c50-9d3c-1987ea50cccf", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Reject legacy packet loads from callbacks\n\ncheck_ld_abs() models a failed BPF_LD_ABS or BPF_LD_IND in a\nsubprogram as an implicit return with R0 set to zero. It calls\nprepare_func_exit() to explore this synthesized path.\n\nWhen the load is reached directly from a synchronous callback,\nprepare_func_exit() enforces the callback return contract and marks R0\nprecise. R0 is not derived from a real instruction on this path, so\nprecision backtracking reaches the callback call with R0 still requested\nand triggers the \"callback unexpected regs\" verifier bug. A privileged\nprogram loader can therefore cause a verifier warning and an -EFAULT\nBPF_PROG_LOAD.\n\nThese legacy packet-load instructions are deprecated. Reject them from\ncallbacks rather than complicating their implicit-return model. Check all\nactive frames before constructing the implicit return so nested static\nsubprograms cannot hide the callback context.\n\nGlobal functions are verified independently with a fresh frame zero, so\nan active-frame check cannot identify a global function called from a\ncallback. Also check the complete subprogram call graph during stack-depth\nvalidation and reject a function containing a legacy load when any caller\nis a callback. This covers global and static descendants without making\nhas_ld_abs transitive, preserving its per-function BTF return-type check.\nOrdinary uses outside callbacks remain supported.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:12", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cebda2a2bb4183550eae9dcf888c16407b4fffda", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3484a99303912db62428494a9061212049027e57", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bc489c0c9b8c86bd7fac42cfd1bb152f042fca56", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7d28823c662128caae63f14e16bd394916c139b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wq8m-pjjr-x46w", "CVE-2026-98044"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d91bd37-380a-3858-b504-5299931c7444", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.148 <6.7"}, {"id": "0f4d0a16-a135-358b-91b3-df5f10994d40", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "19fbcf64-4f00-3d1f-8025-891347f96f9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18.42 <6.18.53"}, {"id": "2310306b-8d07-3be6-88e9-b5250ba8ea5d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ee861486e377edc55361c08dcbceab3f6b6577bd <bc489c0c9b8c86bd7fac42cfd1bb152f042fca56"}, {"id": "27159837-9c3f-356c-b9cb-dc85923a2fa1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de1055e7f9e67af32b1f3376066272b04e5223c0"}, {"id": "2922a7e8-36d7-3f28-b2d9-b6ba36f9d291", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1"}, {"id": "37de8e6d-4c7a-3304-acf7-67686cf43a28", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8674e2db06cff6b50f2216eed9a761d15425bb34 <cebda2a2bb4183550eae9dcf888c16407b4fffda"}, {"id": "44d8ec20-7a34-35b3-b980-9c434983a971", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ee861486e377edc55361c08dcbceab3f6b6577bd <e7d28823c662128caae63f14e16bd394916c139b"}, {"id": "5cd75b0a-51f9-3310-9eef-22d4e3ddb091", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.265 <5.11"}, {"id": "5e6916d8-eede-3694-a5d9-59e45844e05a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.101 <6.12.114"}, {"id": "91bb489c-d9ca-3e51-95cb-29ed92252ff8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "928d354ae3557e8f755a227e67be88034eb3cd7f"}, {"id": "9e226193-0473-3e20-99ae-123602754068",